  "raw": {
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4184163": {
      "title": "Accounts Payable and Business Office Coordinator",
      "description": "Accounts Payable and Business Office Coordinator. Mount Mary University. Position Summary Under the direction of the Accounting Manager, the Accounts Payable and Business Office Coordinator performs full-cycle accounts payable duties and provides front-line support for student accounts, cash receipts, and general Business Office operations. The position is responsible for processing invoices and payments accurately and on time, maintaining vendor and payment records, supporting expense and credit-card processing, assisting students and employees with account questions, and completing daily cash- receipt and deposit activities. The position works closely with the Business Office, Financial Aid, Advancement, Registrar, and other University departments and handles confidential financial information with integrity and sound internal controls. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Accounts Payable Receive, review, code, verify, and process invoices, check requests, and other payment documentation in accordance with University policies and approval requirements. Manage the invoice workflow and communicate with department managers regarding timely submission, coding, documentation, and approval of invoices. Prepare and distribute weekly accounts payable payments and related reports; maintain accurate records of invoices, payments, credits, and expenditures. Review and process employee expense reimbursements, purchasing-card and credit-card activity, and supporting documentation. Maintain vendor records, including W-9 collection, new-vendor setup, vendor changes, and annual 1099 preparation and processing. Research and resolve invoice discrepancies, duplicate payments, vendor statement differences, credit memos, stop payments, and purchase-order amendments. Verify and post accounts payable transactions to the accounting system and assist with reconciliations, month-end close, audit requests, and record retention. Regularly review accounts payable procedures, recommend process improvements, and train employees on invoice and payment processes. Student Accounts, Cash Receipts, and Billing Support Serve as a primary Business Office contact for students and families regarding account balances, monthly statements, payment activity, payment plans, and Transact or myMountMary account questions. Research and help resolve student-account issues in coordination with Business Office accountants, Financial Aid, the Registrar, and other departments. Maintain payment plans, update billing schedules, prepare monthly invoices and correspondence, and assist in preparing current and former student accounts for collection activity. Receive and accurately record student tuition payments and other University receipts, including online and in-person payments. Post and close daily cash receipts, prepare deposits, maintain the daily deposit worksheet, and support reconciliation of receipt activity. Maintain campus petty cash in accordance with University policy and provide appropriate documentation and balancing . Setup and run student charges including student billing. Business Office Service and Administrative Support Provide welcoming, timely , and professional service to students, faculty, staff, vendors, and other internal and external customers. Answer the main Business Office telephone and email and provide front-desk coverage during designated office hours. Protect confidential student, employee, banking, vendor, and University information. Apply University policies and procedures fairly and consistently and promptly elevate exceptions or control concerns. Proactively support Business Office workflow, cross-train in related functions, and perform other duties, special projects, or responsibilities as assigned. Internal Control Expectation: The position follows established segregation-of-duties requirements and may not approve its own transactions, independently authorize vendor banking changes, or release payments without required secondary approval. Qualifications and Experience Associate degree in accounting, business, finance, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. At least two years of accounts payable, accounting, student accounts, cashiering, or comparable Business Office experience; higher-education experience is preferred. Working knowledge of accounting fundamentals, accounts payable practices, documentation standards, and basic internal controls. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, and experience using accounting, ERP, invoice-workflow, payment, or database systems; Jenzabar and Transact experience is preferred. Strong attention to detail, numerical accuracy, organization, prioritization, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills and demonstrated customer-service ability with diverse students, employees, managers, and vendors. Ability to manage recurring deadlines and interruptions in a fast-paced, multi-tasked environment. Demonstrated integrity, discretion, and ability to handle confidential information. Equal Opportunity Employment Mount Mary University practices equal opportunity employment as part of its ongoing commitment to diversity in the workplace. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position."
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/3934867": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor – BSN Program PT",
      "description": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor – BSN Program PT. Mount Mary University. Position Summary Mount Mary University invites applications for Adjunct Clinical Instructors to support the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) program. Clinical faculty play a crucial role in guiding students in real-world practice settings, fostering professional growth, clinical reasoning, and compassionate patient-centered care. This role focuses exclusively on clinical teaching and supervision, with no didactic responsibilities required. Primary Responsibilities · Supervise and evaluate students in clinical settings such as Long-Term Care, Medical–Surgical, or other assigned practice areas. · Provide on-site coaching, clinical demonstrations, and real-time competency assessment. · Ensure safe, ethical, evidence-based practice aligned with course and program outcomes. · Conduct pre- and post-clinical conferences to enhance clinical reflection and judgment. · Provide timely, constructive feedback and complete required student evaluations. · Communicate effectively with clinical partners and uphold institutional and regulatory expectations. · Foster an inclusive learning environment that supports diverse learners. · Participate in required faculty onboarding and orientation Qualifications · BSN required; MSN preferred for clinical instruction. · Unencumbered RN license in Wisconsin (or eligibility for WI licensure). · Minimum of two years of clinical practice experience in the assigned specialty area. · Prior experience precepting or teaching students is desirable. · Strong communication, professionalism, and commitment to student success."
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/3926555": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Biology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Biology - Milwaukee, WI - Mount Mary University Jobs Jobs Login Back to all jobs Adjunct Faculty - Biology Menomonee River Pkwy, Milwaukee, WI 53222, USA, 53222 Part Time Email Me Similar Jobs Email Me This Job Adjunct Position in Biology School of Arts and Sciences Mount Mary University, Wisconsin's oldest Catholic University for women, is seeking individuals to contribute to the realization of our mission through teaching courses in the Biology Program in the Spring 2026 semester (Jan. 17 – May 16, 2025). The following course is available: BIO 100 – Intro Cell & Molecular Biology & Lab (4cr, compensated at 6cr for lab work), meets Tuesday/Thursday at 1 pm – 3:50 pm At minimum a master's degree in biology or comparable field is required. With current enrollment of about 1,400, Mount Mary University \"provides an environment for the development of the whole person.\" The University encourages leadership, integrity, and a deep sense of social justice arising from a sensitivity to moral values and Christian principles. The undergraduate curriculum integrates the liberal arts with professional preparation. Mount Mary is an equal opportunity employer as part of our ongoing commitment to diversity in our workplace. We will begin to review applications immediately. Candidates will be contacted for interviews. Prior teaching experience is desirable. Qualified applicants should submit the following: A letter of application detailing compatibility with posted requirements A current resume or CV, with previous teaching experience detailed A list of professional references For questions, please reach out to the chair of the Division of Math & Science, Jeremy Edison, PhD. Mount Mary University welcomes and encourages applications from qualified candidates and all will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, ethnicity, pregnancy, disability, genetic information, or any other groups protected by law. Mount Mary seeks to hire and retain personnel who will make a positive contribution to its mission, vision, and values. THIS POSITION HAS BEEN CLOSED! PLEASE CHOOSE ONE OF THE OPTIONS BELOW: Search Jobs Search Current Openings Sign Up For Job Alerts! Name You must type a name. Email You must type a valid email. Location (city, state or zip code) You must select a location. Accept Terms of Service I agree to the terms of service and privacy policy. You must accept the terms of service and privacy policy. Send Me Jobs Would you like Refer.io to send you similar jobs from other employers? Yes, daily! Yes, weekly! No, thanks. Please type the job title you are interested in: Job title You must type a job title. We'll send some jobs to you in the next 30 minutes. If you don't see them, check your spam folder. Next Resume Input Select file Resume File You must select a file. Upload Resume upload later Thank you for subscribing to receive job alerts. You should start receiving emails in the next week. Your file is uploading. Please wait a few seconds. Enter your phone number if you'd like to receive job alerts for in via text message. Phone number You must type a phone number. Please indicate if you agree to Refer.io's Subscriber Communication Policy . Please indicate if you agree to Refer.io's Subscriber Communication Policy. Select an option Yes, I agree to be contacted by text messages No, I do not agree to receive text messages You must agree to our Subscriber Communication Policy in order to receive text messages from Refer.io. Yes, why not? Not now Refer.io can assist in your job search. Please answer the following questions to amplify your search results. Education status Education status In School Graduated Never Attended Partially completed You must select an education status answer. Work status Work status Currently employed Out of work Temporary job You must select a work status answer. Job search status Job search status Actively looking for a job Passively looking for a job Not looking for a job You must select a job search status answer. Seeking for Employment goal Similar Job to What I Do Now Progress to a Higher Job in the Same Field Jump to a New Field of Work You must select a seeking status answer. Job type Job type Full Time Part Time From Home You must select a job type answer. Next powered by Refer.io Refer.io Hiring Software Maintained by isolved Talent Acquisition - © 2026 Refresh Search the FAQ here Go Common Job Questions"
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4231367": {
      "title": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty – Clinical, Lab, and Theory",
      "description": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty – Clinical, Lab, and Theory. Mount Mary University. Adjunct Nursing Faculty – Clinical, Lab, and Theory Position Summary Mount Mary University invites applications for Adjunct Nursing Faculty to support the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) program in clinical, nursing skills laboratory, and/or theory (didactic) instruction . Adjunct faculty play an important role in preparing students for professional nursing practice by fostering clinical judgment, critical thinking, skill development, professional growth, and compassionate, patient-centered care. Adjunct assignments may include clinical instruction in healthcare settings, instruction and supervision in nursing skills laboratories, and/or classroom-based theory instruction based on faculty qualifications, expertise, program needs, and course availability. Primary Responsibilities Depending on assigned instructional responsibilities, adjunct nursing faculty may perform some or all of the following: Clinical Instruction Supervise and evaluate students in clinical settings such as long-term care, medical-surgical, community, or other assigned practice areas. Provide on-site coaching, clinical demonstrations, and real-time assessment of student performance and competency. Ensure safe, ethical, evidence-based nursing practice aligned with course and program outcomes. Conduct pre- and post-clinical conferences to promote reflection, clinical reasoning, and clinical judgment. Provide timely, constructive feedback and complete required student evaluations. Communicate effectively and professionally with clinical partners, course faculty, and nursing program leadership. Nursing Skills Laboratory Instruction Facilitate student learning and skill development in the nursing skills laboratory. Demonstrate and reinforce evidence-based nursing skills, assessment techniques, and safe patient-care practices. Supervise student practice and provide coaching and feedback during skills development and competency validation. Evaluate student performance during skills practice, checkoffs, and other laboratory-based learning activities as assigned. Reinforce connections between nursing theory, clinical judgment, and hands-on patient-care skills. Maintain a safe, organized learning environment and promote appropriate use of laboratory equipment and supplies. Collaborate with course faculty to ensure laboratory instruction is consistent with course objectives, program expectations, and current nursing practice standards. Theory/Didactic Instruction Provide classroom-based instruction in assigned nursing courses consistent with established course objectives and BSN program outcomes. Prepare and deliver engaging, evidence-based instruction using appropriate teaching and learning strategies. Facilitate development of clinical judgment, critical thinking, and application of nursing knowledge to patient-care situations. Assess student learning through examinations, assignments, case studies, classroom activities, or other approved evaluation methods. Provide timely grading and constructive feedback to students. Maintain appropriate course documentation and communicate student progress or concerns with program leadership. Collaborate with nursing faculty to promote consistency across theory, laboratory, and clinical components of the curriculum. General Faculty Responsibilities Foster an inclusive, respectful learning environment that supports diverse learners. Maintain professional, ethical, and academic standards consistent with University, School of Nursing, regulatory, and accreditation expectations. Communicate promptly and professionally with students, faculty, staff, and external partners. Participate in required faculty onboarding, orientation, training, and course-specific preparation. Utilize University learning management systems and other instructional technology as required. Maintain current knowledge and competence within the assigned area of nursing practice and instruction. Qualifications Clinical and Nursing Skills Laboratory Adjunct Faculty BSN required; MSN preferred. Current, unencumbered RN license in Wisconsin or eligibility for Wisconsin RN licensure. Minimum of two years of nursing practice experience; experience should be relevant to the assigned instructional area. Prior experience teaching, precepting, mentoring, or supervising nursing students or nurses is desirable. Theory/Didactic Adjunct Faculty MSN required. Current, unencumbered RN license in Wisconsin or eligibility for Wisconsin RN licensure. Nursing practice experience relevant to the assigned course or content area. Previous classroom, academic, or nursing education experience preferred. All Adjunct Nursing Faculty Strong communication, collaboration, organization, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated professionalism and commitment to student learning and success. Ability to effectively support students with varying levels of experience and diverse learning needs. Commitment to evidence-based nursing education and professional nursing standards. Adjunct assignments are based on program needs, faculty qualifications, area of expertise, and course availability. Candidates may be considered for clinical, laboratory, theory, or a combination of instructional assignments based on their education and experience."
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4140461": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - Interior Architecture & Design",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant - Interior Architecture & Design. Mount Mary University. Position Summary : Mount Mary University seeks an individual to provide part-time administrative and technical support to the Interior Architecture & Design Program. This person is responsible for maintaining a flow of persons and communications for the Interior Architecture & Design Program, while performing a wide variety of office management and accreditation functions for the Chair, faculty and students. This person must be able to work independently on multiple, diverse projects and contribute the realization of the University's mission. Primary Responsibilities: Duties include, but are not limited to, the following: Maintain a welcoming and supportive office to aid faculty and students in a collaborative and collegial environment. This position requires diplomacy, proactive thinking, and calm action in assisting the Chair, faculty, and students. Coordinate and facilitate communications among the program, the University, and the interior design community at large. Use Microsoft Excel to manage, track, and organize data. Use Microsoft Outlook for scheduling and calendar management. Use Microsoft Teams to manage program files. Use Microsoft 365 and other software to generate letters, reports, labels, and online forms. Use Jenzabar software to compile reports and complete queries and data entry. Facilitate the use of technology to improve workflow and data collection and management in collaboration with IT. Organize and maintain records and files; establish and maintain confidential files for the program, assessment, accreditation activities, and program review documentation. Support the Chair in writing student communications regarding events and advising in collaboration with other university programs. Coordinate with the Marketing Department to act as content manager for the Program's webpage. Act as liaison to IT, Public Safety and Buildings and Grounds departments to report and monitor online work orders on behalf of the Chair and faculty until work orders have been resolved. Collect and deliver campus mail; facilitate bulk mailings. Manage and track the program's budget expenditures, faculty reimbursements, reconcile expense reports for faculty, prepare check requests and monitor budgets. Support Chair and faculty before, during, and after special events, field trips, industry engagements, and student activities. This may include preparing invitations, announcements, certificates, display information, manage catering and space reservations, and complete any follow-up correspondence. Monitor and purchase supplies as needed or directed. Develop, document, and maintain administrative procedures, workflows, and systems that support operational efficiency and accountability. Skills and Experience: B.A. degree or equivalent preferred. Minimum of 3 years of administrative experience working in an administrative support role with ability to work with modest supervision. Experience using Microsoft Excel including organizing and cleaning data, filtering and sorting data, creating visual representations of data, using formulas, and working with tables and pivot tables. Excellent skills in Microsoft 365, including Outlook, Teams, and Word, and ability to learn new software as needed. Proficiency in Jenzabar preferred. Ability to independently regulate workflow and prioritize tasks to support competing deadlines and workflow. Strong, customer service orientation with sincere desire to assist faculty and students. Outstanding written and verbal communication skills. Attention to detail. Able to demonstrate poise and professionalism under stress. Cooperative, friendly, and professional manner. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality and professional demeanor. Commitment to working as a team member and working with diverse constituencies and within tight timeframes. Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to build relationships with other University academic and support services departments. Flexibility in schedule to support special events on an occasional basis"
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4094462": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Engagement - FT",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Student Engagement - FT. Mount Mary University. Position Summary: The Assistant Director of Student Engagement provides strategic leadership and direction in the university's efforts to enhance student engagement and involvement towards ultimately increasing student success and retention. This professional will have a unique opportunity to lead in the delivery of highly effective student engagement programs and services that promote equity, inclusion, sense of belonging, and social justice, to an increasingly diverse student population. The Assistant Director will also collaborate with professionals across the university to promote holistic student development. Mount Mary University serves an undergraduate population with over 60% of students identifying from historically marginalized backgrounds Primary Responsibilities: Develop and implement co-curricular campus programs that promote the holistic development of students, build community, increase a sense of belonging, meet the needs of our diverse student population, and support the University's mission. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and students to develop robust student development programs that positively impact persistence and retention such as the Mount Mary Moments series. Collaborate with the Director of First Year and Transition Programs to develop, implement, and evaluate a comprehensive program to engage first year students, towards encouraging student success, including New Student Registration and Orientation. Hire, train, supervise, and evaluate professional and student (Graduate Assistants and Program Assistants) staff. Manage Student Engagement social media connections with students, including Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram Facilitate programs that create a vibrant and welcoming atmosphere, promote social justice, and multi-cultural competence among students on campus. Advise the Student Government Association and supervise student organizations. Foster the development of new clubs and organizations, and provide training and enrichment for student leaders and their organizations' advisors. Develop, monitor, and revise policies for the operation and oversight of student clubs and organizations. Communication with vendors and others on campus. Participate in the shared professional staff on-call schedule, providing crisis response, support and referrals. Maintain an active presence and engagement with students, including evenings and weekends as needed. Other duties as assigned by supervisor. Other Administrative Responsibilities: Provide reports to the senior leadership of Student Affairs as required. Manage budgets assigned to the Engagement department. Collaborate on the development of university-wide policies that affect students. Perform other duties, responsibilities, or special projects as assigned Skills and Experience : Bachelor's degree required. Master's degree preferred, preferably in Student Affairs, Higher Education, or College Student Personnel Administration Experience developing and implementing a wide range of successful programs at the college level Experience advising student clubs and organizations preferred Experience with developing new student orientation and first year student programs and services. Demonstrated commitment to promoting equity and inclusion; experience working with underrepresented students Exceptional ability to multitask and prioritize projects Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to work with diverse groups, facilitate group process and foster collaborative decision making Physical Demands: May be required to lift up to 20 lbs. Must reach, bend, stoop, lift Must sit, walk, or stand Some repetitive motion may be required Working Conditions: Can regularly be scheduled for 45+ hours a week Varying workflow; sometimes stressful with high workload times of the year Complete work required within a limited space Complete work required within a limited time Mount Mary University practices equal opportunity employment as part of our ongoing commitment to diversity in our workplace."
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4180546": {
      "title": "Dean School of Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Dean School of Arts & Sciences. Mount Mary University. Position Summary : The Dean of Arts & Sciences possesses exceptional knowledge and skills to advance the distinctive mission and values (Competence, Community, Compassion & Commitment) of Mount Mary University. The Dean provides a supportive climate informed by a deep understanding of diversity, equity and inclusion practices that foster collaboration between Schools and the larger University community. They demonstrate outstanding qualities in leadership, collegiality, teaching, professional development, and community service. The Dean must work effectively with internal and external constituencies to establish strategic partnerships across disciplines. The Dean must have knowledge of and ability to support programmatic and University accreditation. They work with the University's Administration, Alumni & Donor Relations Office, and Faculty to identify and cultivate donor prospects and grant opportunities. The Dean will provide overall direction for budgetary and fiscal affairs and will be responsible for the financial viability of academic programs and the Institution at large. They must be an articulate representative and advocate for the School of Arts & Sciences and University. The Dean reports directly to and collaborates closely with the Vice President for Academic Affairs Primary Responsibilities: •Provides collaborative support to the Division Chairs and faculty in the form of collegial, transparent communication; •Leads the School of Arts & Sciences in strategic planning initiatives targeting accreditation, curriculum and co-curriculum development, enrollment growth, retention and persistence efforts, and cost effectiveness. Utilizes and accurately interprets metrics provided by the Institutional Effectiveness and Business Offices to ensure academic quality and integrity of programs; •Works collaboratively with Division Chairs to develop and maintain budgets and is responsible for the overall management of fiscal resources of the School; •Serves as a visible leader of the School of Arts & Sciences and develops relationships with corporate and community partners to establish internships and other applied academic opportunities. Proactively seeks out fundraising and grant opportunities that will further strategic initiatives working collaboratively with the Director of Grants Management, faculty, Alumnae & Donor Relations, and University Marketing & Communications staff; •Works in joint partnership with academic programs to utilize discipline-specific expertise that will facilitate innovative change. Works with deans and faculty in other academic Schools to further interdisciplinary collaboration and efficiencies across core curriculum course content and offerings. •Collaborate with Student Affairs administration and Student Success Program staff to provide support services and faculty professional development that strengthens academic experiences and creates student sense of belonging; •Works with the faculty to develop and propose new programs, and to facilitate required approval processes for new academic programs. Works with Division Chairs and the Registrar's Office to ensure integration of changes into the overall curriculum and the University Catalog; •Provides oversight and overall coordination of course schedules constructed by the Division Chairs and in collaboration with the other School Deans; •Advocates for academic technology that will enhance the integrity of discipline-specific curriculum; Reviews Core and program assessment of student learning outcomes prepared by faculty at the end of each academic year to ensure that they are complete and accurate. Assists chairs and faculty in coordinating Program Reviews, writes an evaluative summary of the final product and reviews annual updates before submitting to the Vice President for Academic Affairs; •Serves on search committees for full-time faculty in the School of Arts & Sciences and works with Division Chairs and Human Resources to process employment agreements for adjunct faculty with other School Deans. Provides support to the Division Chairs to coordinate resources for new faculty (e.g., office space, computers, keys, etc.); •Attends regular meetings and participates in Deans Council. Coordinates and leads regular Division Chair/Faculty meetings in the school, including those associated with accreditation. Ensures that there is timely communication between appropriate constituencies about action items that arise •Serves on University committees and taskforces as needed •Attends programmatic Advisory Board meetings. Provides support to assess Advisory Board related initiatives for alignment with the University's strategic plan; •Works collaboratively with constituencies, providing ongoing mentoring for full-time tenure-track faculty to meet promotion and tenure criteria. Focus on encouraging teaching excellence, University and community service, scholarship, and professional development. Evaluates portfolios for Division Chairs applying for promotion and tenure. Writes letters of recommendation as appropriate for School faculty applying for promotion and tenure. Provides general support and mentoring for all department members including non-tenure track and adjunct faculty •Conducts first semester classroom evaluations for all new faculty. Reviews all scheduled evaluations including Faculty Records and course evaluations. Conducts yearly evaluation of Division Chairs as part of Faculty Record review; •Supervises and evaluates Administrative Assistants and staff; •Facilitates the resolution of disagreements and conflicts that involve students, faculty, and staff in accordance with documented University policies and procedures in alignment with the Mission and values of the University •Supervises the Director of Scholarships and Study Abroad and oversees the scheduling, planning, and following of policies and procedures of study abroad programs •Co-leads Academic Standing Review at the end of the fall and spring semesters, ensuring that students' academic status (academic probation or dismissal) is consistently updated and communicated as defined by the policies and procedures in the Academic Catalog. Reviews academic dismissal appeals and reinstatement decisions with the Committee of School Deans •Plans and leads the University's annual Scholars' Day in collaboration with the other school deans and administrative assistants, including the annual Awards and Honors Society Inductions Ceremony •Facilitates training and professional development for faculty on academic advising, vocational discernment, and teaching pedagogy topics as needed •Attends and participates in School events to support student and faculty accomplishments, including but not limited to capstone presentations, gallery exhibits, and the annual student-produced fashion show •Perform other duties, responsibilities, or special projects as assigned Skills and Experience: •A PhD or terminal degree that aligns with discipline or profession included in the School of Arts & Sciences is required; •A record of excellence in teaching, service, and professional development that meet criteria established by Mount Mary University; •Extensive knowledge and practice of diversity, equity and inclusive excellence pedagogies that create a sense of belonging for all students, faculty, and staff at the University; •A minimum of five years of exemplary administrative experience in higher education; •Exceptional written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills; •Ability to manage stress with multiple competing priorities while maintaining a positive attitude and effect; •Self-motivated, and self-directed to design and complete complex projects in a timely manner; •Outstanding skills in critical and creative thinking, as well as independent decision making; •Evidence of the ability to establish external relationships that strengthen academic programming; •Ability to conduct financial analyses and interpret a wide array of institutional data; •Understanding of general accounting principles to manage budgets and ensure fiscal responsibility; •Demonstrated competence in the use of academic technology. •The ability to work with diverse groups, facilitate group process and foster collaborative decision making Qualifications: •To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each primary duties satisfactorily. The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform primary functions. Physical Demands: •May be required to lift up to 20 lbs. •Must reach, bend, stoop, lift •Must sit, walk or stand •Some repetitive motion may be required Working Conditions: •Can be scheduled for up to 40 hours a week •Varying workflow; sometimes stressful with high workload times of the year •Complete work required within a limited space •Complete work required within a limited time Mount Mary University encourages applications from all qualified candidates and is vitally committed to all aspects of diversity, equity and inclusion. We welcome and encourage applications from qualified candidates and all will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, ethnicity, pregnancy, disability, genetic information or any other groups protected by law. Mount Mary seeks to hire and retain personnel who will make a positive contribution to its mission, vision and values."
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4184360": {
      "title": "Director of Relationship Violence, Sexual Assault, and Stalking Services - FT",
      "description": "Director of Relationship Violence, Sexual Assault, and Stalking Services - FT. Mount Mary University. Position Overview: Mount Mary University seeks a strategic, compassionate, and culturally responsive leader to serve as the Director of Relationship Violence, Sexual Assault, and Stalking Services. This position leads the Soaring Above: Blue Angels' Strategies to Reduce DVSAS on Campus initiative, funded by the U.S. Department of Justice Office on Violence Against Women (OVW). The Director is responsible for implementing a trauma-informed, prevention-based, and collaborative approach that shifts campus culture, builds capacity, and reduces the incidence of domestic violence, dating violence, sexual assault, and stalking (DVSAS) through education, outreach, and systems-level change. Key Responsibilities: Capacity Building & Collaboration Lead the development and implementation of comprehensive campus-wide strategies to build institutional capacity for preventing and responding to DVSAS. Chair and coordinate the Coordinated Community Response Team (CCRT), ensuring diverse representation from students, staff, faculty, and community partners. Cultivate partnerships with culturally specific service providers to ensure accessible and inclusive services for all students, especially those from underserved populations. Facilitate cross-departmental collaboration, integrating public safety, residential life, counseling services, and campus ministry into prevention and response efforts. Program Oversight & Compliance Manage all aspects of the OVW Campus Grant project including reporting, budget alignment, training compliance, and documentation. Serve as liaison with OVW program staff and technical assistance providers. Ensure implementation aligns with federal guidelines, MMU & SSND mission, and grant deliverables. Prevention, Education, and Training Lead the development and implementation of a trauma-informed, culturally relevant prevention curriculum designed to reach 100% of MMU students through required programming, workshops, and classroom integration. Design and facilitate professional development and training opportunities for students, staff, faculty, and campus leadership on topics such as healthy relationships, boundaries, trauma response, LGBTQ+ inclusion, and bystander intervention. Direct Support Services & Advocacy Coordinate confidential, student-centered services including warm referrals, advocacy, and support tailored to individual needs. Lead efforts to remove barriers to reporting and service access through culturally responsive and identity-affirming outreach. Assist in policy updates and campus-wide initiatives that promote equity, accountability, and healing-centered practices. Program Evaluation & Sustainability Track program outcomes, gather qualitative and quantitative data, and use findings to continuously improve services and engagement. Contribute to long-term sustainability planning through institutional buy-in, resource development, and systemic integration. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in social work, psychology, public health, education, or a related field, or commensurate experience. Master's degree preferred. Demonstrated commitment to trauma-informed, survivor-centered, and culturally responsive practices. Experience working with diverse student populations, including BIPOC, LGBTQ+, first-generation, and commuter students. Strong leadership and facilitation skills, with a proven ability to manage projects and build collaborative teams. Familiarity with Title IX, Clery Act, and federal violence prevention guidelines preferred. Bilingual candidates strongly encouraged to apply. Mount Mary University welcomes and encourages applications from qualified candidates and all will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, ethnicity, pregnancy, disability, genetic information, or any other groups protected by law. Mount Mary seeks to hire and retain personnel who will make a positive contribution to its mission, vision, and values."
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4008209": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor. Mount Mary University. Position Title: Financial Aid Counselor Reports To : Director of Financial Aid & Veterans Services Department: Financial Aid & Veterans Services Employment Status: Full-time Pay Months: July-June Position Summary: The position of Financial Aid Counselor is an integral part of Mount Mary University's student enrollment and retention team, which requires an enthusiastic, high-energy individual. The individual must be committed to personal attention and follow up with prospective and enrolled students. The Financial Aid Counselor will work closely with the Director of Financial Aid & Veterans Services to ensure that the Financial Aid & Veterans Services Office and its services play an efficient and successful part in the recruitment and retention of Mount Mary students. Primary Responsibilities: Counsel students and parents regarding financial aid award offers, eligibility, and processes Provide information to students on aggregate limits for Federal and State programs Conduct financial aid workshops and presentations Complete verification and awarding of financial aid to students Manage Federal and Private Loan Program Assist as required with annual audits Process and award outside scholarship checks Performs other duties as assigned Experience and Qualifications • Bachelor's Degree required • Previous experience as a Financial Aid Administrator preferred • Outstanding written and verbal communication skills; must be able to communicate and interact effectively with prospective and current students • Strong interpersonal and organizational skills necessary • Bilingual in Spanish a plus Physical Demands: • May be required to lift up to 20 lbs. • Must reach, bend, stoop, lift • Must sit, walk or stand • Some repetitive motion may be required Working Conditions: • Can be scheduled for up to 40 hours a week, including occasional evenings and weekends. • Varying workflow; sometimes stressful with high workload times of the year. Mount Mary University welcomes and encourages applications from qualified candidates and all will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, ethnicity, pregnancy, disability, genetic information, or any other groups protected by law. Mount Mary seeks to hire and retain personnel who will make a positive contribution to its mission, vision, and values."
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4184449": {
      "title": "Licensed Professional Counselor - FT",
      "description": "Licensed Professional Counselor - FT. Mount Mary University. Position Summary: The Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) will provide oversight to the operation and management of the Mount Mary University (MMU) Counseling and Wellness Center (CWC). Current licensure as a licensed LPC in Wisconsin is required. Duties include clinical supervision for both master's and doctoral students, development of policies and procedures, and collaboration with other units on campus. Primary Responsibilities: Maintain an active caseload Clinical supervision to doctoral and/or master's-level counseling students, as well as, graduate assistants assigned to the CWC. Demonstrate a strong commitment to multicultural and social justice counseling competencies as evidenced in clinical work and supervision. Collaborate (via the prescribed evaluation process) with the Practicum and Internship Coordinator to ensure that both master's and doctoral-level student interns reach developmentally appropriate clinical competency. Ability to work collegially in a collaborative team environment. Provide leadership within a counseling clinic, including the ability to promote the CWC and develop partnerships and collaborate with stakeholders within the university and the local community. Development and oversight of CWC policies and procedures. Monitor compliance with legal and ethical issues, and quality standards of trainees within the CWC. Review and approve case notes and treatment plans of counselors-in-training. Perform other duties, responsibilities, or special projects as assigned. Skills and Experience : Experience working in a University counseling center or with young adults. Experience as a Licensed Professional Counselor. Strong working knowledge and understanding of established professional codes of ethics and best practices in multicultural and social justice competencies and supervision. Demonstrated commitment to promoting inclusiveness and cultural competence; experience working with underrepresented students and students from at-risk backgrounds. Experience and understanding of current issues and developments in higher education. Outstanding verbal, writing, and presentation skills; must be able to communicate and interact effectively with MMU students, employees, and alum. Exceptional ability to multitask and prioritize projects. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to work with diverse groups, facilitate group processes and foster collaborative decision-making. Qualifications: Master's degree required. Be a Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) in Wisconsin in good standing A counselor-first professional identity as evidenced via credentials and engagement with professional counseling organizations preferred. Experience in Institution of Higher Education or College Counseling Center setting preferred. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each primary duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform primary functions. Mount Mary University encourages applications from all qualified candidates and is vitally committed to all aspects of diversity, equity, and inclusion. We welcome and encourage applications from qualified candidates and all will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, ethnicity, pregnancy, disability, genetic information, or any other groups protected by law. Mount Mary seeks to hire and retain personnel who will make a positive contribution to its mission, vision, and values. For more information about diversity, equity, and inclusion at Mount Mary please visit http://www.mtmary.edu/about/diversity"
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4202255": {
      "title": "Marketing Manager",
      "description": "Marketing Manager. Mount Mary University. Position Summary: The Marketing Manager for University Marketing and Communications at Mount Mary University serves as a strategic leader responsible for directing the Marketing team to elevate the institution's regional profile. In this role, the manager oversees the development and execution of a bold, unified brand identity across digital advertising, traditional media, and public relations initiatives. To ensure marketing efforts align with broader institutional goals, the position actively collaborates with key internal partners including Recruitment, Academic Deans, Alumnae Relations, and Development to craft targeted campaigns that drive enrollment, donor engagement, and community awareness. Ultimately, the role combines hands-on project management with team leadership to deliver cohesive, high-impact communications to both internal and external audiences. Primary Responsibilities: Marketing Oversee the development, implementation and management of a comprehensive integrated communications and marketing program; the strategic program will encompass branding, recruitment marketing, media relations, and digital or physical publications. Has oversight for the development and implementation of marketing programs (i.e. advertising, direct marketing, digital advertisements) to effectively market the University to various communities. Works with the Vice President for Enrollment and Marketing Communications to develop themes and/or messages to promote University priorities for use by all campus offices engaged in student, community, alumni, and development outreach. Support the development of unified campus-wide comprehensive marketing plan as well as marketing theme and designs, including logos, and other creative designs. Directs the development of collateral materials in support of marketing strategies including publications, videos, electronic communications and multimedia presentations. Identifies target groups for campus outreach and dissemination of marketing materials and develops and implements plans for conducting market research of target groups. Oversees the University's relationship with the Agency of Record. Communications Collaborates with the communication staff responsible for media relations and institutional publications for the campus. Including, the development and implementation of a comprehensive integrated communications plan for the campus, in consultation with the President, VP's, Deans, and campus administration. Provides editorial support for the University magazine, and for various campus brochures and newsletters. Develops and implements plans for high visibility speaking engagements and other public relations activities to strategically link the institution and its key leaders with opinion leaders and targeted constituent groups. Media Relations Manages the public information functions for the campus including developing public information policies and ensuring that the office complies with state and federal laws. Drafts and maintains a crisis communication plan and provides crisis communication management for leadership during incidents that have potential to negatively impact the University's reputation. Advises University administrators, staff, and faculty in media relations techniques by providing training exercises and materials. Proactively seeks national news media coverage in concert with campus communication objectives. Supports the coordination of media coverage and responses to major news and events by consulting with appropriate administrators to determine the campus responses and development of position statements. Serves as principal spokesperson for the campus or delegates that responsibility to appropriate individuals. Leadership Hire, support, train and lead a team of marketing staff to coordinate projects and manage intake of upcoming work to organize institutional priorities. Meets regularly with enrollment leadership staff to support strategic direction and planning for enrollment growth and donor cultivation. Facilitate regular meetings with the Marketing and Communications staff. Coordinate regular meetings with Enrollment leadership team and Advancement team on progress towards conversion goals, project updates and progress towards deadlines. Coordinate campaign management with the Director of Communications and the Vice President for Enrollment and Marketing Communications Publications Manages the print and electronic publications function for the campus and supports related staff in the development and distribution of these materials. Advises campus department managers on strategies to communicate with target audiences and development of materials to build the University's image among those audiences. Knowledge of all Microsoft Office software and able to learn and use institutional software systems. Complies with all University policies. Other duties may be assigned. Perform other duties, responsibilities, or special projects as assigned Skills and Experience : Bachelor's degree in communications, public relations, marketing or journalism required. MBA or Master's degree preferred. Minimum of 3 years of marketing/communications experience that includes working with marketing professionals, editors, graphic and Web designers, clients, and media vendors Strong working knowledge and understanding of established professional codes of ethics and best practices for marketing. Demonstrated commitment to promoting inclusiveness and cultural competence; experience working with underrepresented students and students from at-risk backgrounds Experience and understanding of current issues and developments in higher education Outstanding verbal, writing, and presentation skills; must be able to communicate and interact effectively with Mount Mary students, employees, and alumnae Exceptional ability to multitask and prioritize projects Understanding of brand strategy and digital advertising campaign management Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to work with diverse groups, facilitate group process and foster collaborative decision making Strong working knowledge of publication design, print production, and vendor relationships Skills in use of Microsoft Office programs and knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite software (InDesign and Photoshop) Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each primary duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform primary functions. Physical Demands: May be required to lift up to 20 lbs. Must reach, bend, stoop, lift Must sit, walk or stand Some repetitive motion may be required Working Conditions: Varying workflow; sometimes stressful with high workload times of the year Complete work required within a limited space Complete work required within a limited time Mount Mary University encourages applications from all qualified candidates and is vitally committed to all aspects of diversity, equity and inclusion. We welcome and encourage applications from qualified candidates and all will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, ethnicity, pregnancy, disability, genetic information or any other groups protected by law. Mount Mary seeks to hire and retain personnel who will make a positive contribution to its mission, vision and values. For more information about diversity, equity and inclusion at Mount Mary please visit https://www.mtmary.edu/about/diversity"
    },
    "https://mtmary.applicantpro.com/jobs/4177866": {
      "title": "Professional Tutor of Writing and Learning Strategies - PT",
      "description": "Professional Tutor of Writing and Learning Strategies - PT. Mount Mary University. Position Title: Professional Tutor of Writing and Learning Strategies Reports To: Director of Learning Services Services Department: Learning Services Employment Status: Part-time, 15-18 hours/week Position Summary: Provide comprehensive writing and learning strategy support to a diverse student population with varied academic needs. Assist students across the disciplines throughout all levels of the research and writing process Assist students in identifying their individual strengths and skills to make study plans, establish academic goals, and maximize the student's potential Collaborate with Success Advisors and as a team member of the Student Success Center (SSC) Facilitate academic skill building workshops, presentations, and classroom visits Maintain accurate tutoring notes and progress using university software Work with students in person and through online platforms Guide graduate students towards developing a professional written voice with formal language Participate in outreach activities to promote tutoring services and resources Assist in the maintenance and evaluation of tutoring materials, surveys, and services Perform other duties, responsibilities, or special projects as assigned Skills and Experience : Bachelor of Arts degree in English, Writing or Humanities Experience with tutoring via on-line delivery/distance learning strongly preferred Demonstrated commitment to promoting inclusiveness and cultural competence; experience working with underrepresented students and students from at-risk backgrounds Experience and understanding of current issues and developments in higher education Outstanding verbal, writing, and presentation skills; must be able to communicate and interact effectively with Mount Mary students, employees, and alumnae Exceptional ability to multitask and prioritize projects Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform primary duties satisfactorily. The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform primary functions. Physical Demands: Must sit, walk or stand Some repetitive motion may be required Working Conditions: Varying workflow; sometimes stressful with high workload times of the year Mount Mary University practices equal opportunity employment as part of our ongoing commitment to diversity in our workplace. Mount Mary University encourages applications from all qualified candidates and is vitally committed to all aspects of diversity, equity, and inclusion. We welcome and encourage applications from qualified candidates and all will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, ethnicity, pregnancy, disability, genetic information, or any other groups protected by law. Mount Mary seeks to hire and retain personnel who will make a positive contribution to its mission, vision, and values."
